# Release Process

- Always run `git pull` on the target branch before creating a release to ensure the local branch reflects the latest merged changes.
- Release notes, commit messages, and PR descriptions must only cover changes to the repository — features, fixes, and user-facing docs.
- Never mention local settings, workflow rules, process instructions, or tooling configuration in release notes, commits, or PR descriptions.
